IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wcr-dates`

-- Workers Compensation Regulation 2016 (NSW) -- Parts 3 and 4 (pre-injury average weekly earnings, "PIAWE") and Part 5
-- (return to work assistance), as they meet an injured worker.
--
-- SEAT. The injured worker. The insurer's duties (deciding an agreement, acting on a withdrawal, paying an increase,
-- deciding a return to work claim) are encoded as what they mean for the worker: a date, and whether the duty was kept.
-- They are regulative rules (DEONTIC), run by EVALTRACE inside exported questions that take only plain facts.
--
-- Part 4 adjusts "the relevant earning period" of Schedule 3 clause 2(2) of the Workers Compensation Act 1987: "the
-- period of 52 weeks ending immediately before the date of the injury". That Act is deposited beside this subject
-- (subjects/au/nsw/workers-compensation-act-1987/registers/source-bundle/act-1987-070.txt); its words are quoted here
-- because the stable l4 cannot IMPORT across subjects. One employment at a time (fork F4).
--
-- ANSWERS. JUST FALSE where the text's own words say no; NOTHING, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment, where it does not
-- answer on the facts given.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Parts 3, 4 and 5 -- earnings and return to work assistance`

§§ `Duties with deadlines`

DECLARE `Earnings party` IS ONE OF `the worker or the employer`, `the insurer`, `the person the claim is made on`

DECLARE `Earnings act` IS ONE OF
    `apply for approval of the agreement`
    `determine the application`
    `determine the earnings and give notice of the withdrawal`
    `pay the increase`
    `determine the claim by accepting or disputing liability`

-- cl 8J(2) "The application is to be made within 5 days after the initial notification to the insurer of the injury".
-- Day 0 is the day of the initial notification.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Earnings party` `Earnings act`
`cl 8J(2) -- the application for approval of a PIAWE agreement is to be made within 5 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the worker or the employer`
    MUST `apply for approval of the agreement`
    WITHIN 5
    LEST BREACH BY `the worker or the employer` BECAUSE "application for approval of the pre-injury average weekly earnings agreement not made within 5 days after the initial notification of the injury (cl 8J(2))"

-- cl 8K(2) "The insurer is to determine the application within 7 days after receiving the application (except as
-- provided by subclause (3))". (3) moves the start of the 7 days; day 0 is whichever day starts them.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Earnings party` `Earnings act`
`cl 8K(2), (3) -- the insurer is to determine the application within 7 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the insurer`
    MUST `determine the application`
    WITHIN 7
    LEST BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "application for approval of the pre-injury average weekly earnings agreement not determined within 7 days (cl 8K(2), (3))"

-- cl 8M(2) "Within 7 days after receiving notice of the withdrawal, the insurer is to -- (a) determine the amount of the
-- pre-injury average weekly earnings ..., and (b) give the worker and the employer notice in writing of the withdrawal
-- ... and of the amount determined". Day 0 is the day the insurer received the notice of withdrawal.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Earnings party` `Earnings act`
`cl 8M(2) -- the insurer is to determine the earnings and give notice within 7 days of a withdrawal` MEANS
    PARTY `the insurer`
    MUST `determine the earnings and give notice of the withdrawal`
    WITHIN 7
    LEST BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "pre-injury average weekly earnings not determined and notified within 7 days after notice of withdrawal from the agreement (cl 8M(2))"

-- cl 8N(1) "Within 14 days after making a payment increase decision, the insurer must pay to the worker the amount of the
-- increase ... Maximum penalty -- 20 penalty units." Day 0 is the day of the decision.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Earnings party` `Earnings act`
`cl 8N(1) -- the insurer must pay the increase within 14 days of a payment increase decision` MEANS
    PARTY `the insurer`
    MUST `pay the increase`
    WITHIN 14
    LEST BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "increase in weekly payments not paid within 14 days after the payment increase decision: an offence, maximum penalty 20 penalty units (cl 8N(1))"

DECLARE `Return to work claim` IS ONE OF
    `a claim for work assistance with a new employer (s 64B)`
    `a claim for education or training (s 64C)`

-- cl 9(2) "The person on whom a claim for compensation under section 64B ... is made must, within 14 days after the
-- claim is made, determine the claim by accepting, or disputing, liability ..."; cl 10(2) the same for s 64C "within 21
-- days". Day 0 is the day the claim is made.
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Return to work claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days to determine` `the claim` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `a claim for work assistance with a new employer (s 64B)` THEN 14
    WHEN `a claim for education or training (s 64C)` THEN 21

GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Return to work claim`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Earnings party` `Earnings act`
`cl 9(2), 10(2) -- the claim must be determined within 14 or 21 days` `the claim` MEANS
    PARTY `the person the claim is made on`
    MUST `determine the claim by accepting or disputing liability`
    WITHIN `the days to determine` `the claim`
    LEST BREACH BY `the person the claim is made on` BECAUSE "return to work assistance claim not determined by accepting or disputing liability in time (cl 9(2): 14 days; cl 10(2): 21 days)"

DECLARE `What became of the duty` IS ONE OF
    `the duty was kept in time`
    `the duty was not kept in time`
    `the duty is still open and still in time`

-- Runs a duty over what happened. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH: where
-- the act was done, FULFILLED means in time and anything else late; where it was not done, the helper asks whether
-- doing it today would still be in time. It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Earnings party` `Earnings act`
      `the party` IS AN `Earnings party`
      `the act` IS AN `Earnings act`
      `the act has been done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day number of the act` IS A NUMBER
      `the day number of today` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`the outcome of` `the rule` `for` `the party` `doing` `the act` `done` `the act has been done` `on day` `the day number of the act` `today being day` `the day number of today` MEANS
    IF `the act has been done`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day number of the act`), (EVENT `the party` `the act` `the day number of the act`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `the duty was kept in time`
         OTHERWISE `the duty was not kept in time`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day number of today`), (EVENT `the party` `the act` `the day number of today`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `the duty is still open and still in time`
         OTHERWISE `the duty was not kept in time`

-- The day number of a day, counted from day 0 (never below 0).
GIVEN `the day asked about` IS A DATE, `day 0` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day number of` `the day asked about` `from` `day 0` MEANS max 0 (`the days between` `day 0` `and` `the day asked about`)

§§ `Part 3 -- injuries received before 21 October 2019`

`21 October 2019` MEANS `the calendar day` 21 10 2019

GIVEN `the date of my injury` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 4 applies to my injury` `the date of my injury` IF (`21 October 2019` `falls on or before` `the date of my injury`)

-- cl 6 (for 1987 Act s 44C(7), injuries before 21 October 2019, cl 6AA) and cl 8AB (for Sch 3 cl 2(4), injuries on or
-- after that day, cl 8(2)): "the amount of $155 is prescribed as the minimum amount applicable to a worker". Sch 3
-- cl 2(4): "If the amount of a worker's pre-injury average weekly earnings is less than any minimum amount prescribed
-- ..., the amount ... is taken to be that minimum amount."
`the prescribed minimum PIAWE` MEANS 155

@export What are my pre-injury average weekly earnings once the $155 minimum is applied (Regulation cl 6, cl 8AB; 1987 Act Sch 3 cl 2(4))?
GIVEN `my pre-injury average weekly earnings as worked out` IS A NUMBER @desc Your pre-injury average weekly earnings as worked out before any minimum, in dollars a week
GIVETH A NUMBER
`My PIAWE after the minimum` MEANS max `the prescribed minimum PIAWE` `my pre-injury average weekly earnings as worked out`

-- cl 7 "For the purposes of the prescribed number of hours wherever referred to in Schedule 3 to the 1987 Act, 38 hours
-- is prescribed." cl 6AA: Part 3 "applies only to injuries received before 21 October 2019".
@export How many hours a week are "the prescribed number of hours" for my injury (Regulation cl 7)?
GIVEN `the date of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The date you received the injury
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`The prescribed number of hours for my injury` MEANS
    IF `Part 4 applies to my injury` `the date of my injury`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: Part 4 prescribes no number of hours for later injuries)
    ELSE JUST 38

§§ `Part 4 Division 2 -- the relevant earning period (cll 8A-8EA)`

DECLARE `Earning period` HAS
    `the first day of the period` IS A DATE
    `the last day of the period` IS A DATE
    `days excluded inside it` IS A NUMBER
    `days that count` IS A NUMBER

`the first prescribed period starts` MEANS `the calendar day` 23 3 2020
`the first prescribed period ends` MEANS `the calendar day` 14 6 2020
`the second prescribed period starts` MEANS `the calendar day` 15 6 2020
`the second prescribed period ends` MEANS `the calendar day` 27 9 2020

-- The days three inclusive runs of days have in common.
GIVEN `a from` IS A DATE, `a to` IS A DATE, `b from` IS A DATE, `b to` IS A DATE, `c from` IS A DATE, `c to` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days shared by three runs` `a from` `a to` `b from` `b to` `c from` `c to` MEANS
    `the days shared by` `a from` `to` `a to` `with` (`the later day of` `b from` `and` `c from`) `to` (`the earlier day of` `b to` `and` `c to`)

-- Sch 3 cl 2(2) (1987 Act): "the period of 52 weeks ending immediately before the date of the injury (the relevant
-- earning period)": from the injury date minus 364 days to the day before the injury.
-- cl 8A(2): the adjustments are made in the order 8B, 8C, 8D, 8E, 8EA; each later one works on the period as already
-- adjusted (8A(3)). 8D (alignment with the pay period) is the insurer's choice and is asked separately; it is not
-- applied here (fork F5).
-- cl 8B: "if the worker was not engaged in the employment from the beginning of the unadjusted earning period", exclude
-- "any period before the day on which the worker was first engaged".
-- cl 8C: if "during the unadjusted earning period, there was a change of an ongoing nature to the employment arrangement
-- resulting in a financially material change to the earnings", exclude "any period before the change ... occurred".
-- cl 8E: if "during any period of not less than seven consecutive calendar days within the unadjusted earning period --
-- (a) no earnings ... were paid or payable ..., and (b) the worker took a period of unpaid leave ... commencing on the
-- first day of that consecutive period", exclude each day "commencing on the first day of the unpaid leave period and
-- ending immediately before the day on which earnings ... once again became payable". One run of unpaid leave (fork F6).
-- cl 8EA: if a change to the worker's arrangements "as a direct result of the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic" happened in
-- the period and "resulted in a financially material reduction to the total earnings ... during the first prescribed
-- period" (23 March to 14 June 2020), exclude that period; and if it "resulted in no earnings ... for a period of 2 or
-- more days commencing on the first day of the second prescribed period" (15 June 2020), also exclude each day from
-- 15 June 2020 to the earlier of the day before earnings in any employment became payable again and 27 September 2020.
GIVEN `the date of my injury` IS A DATE
      `the day I was first engaged` IS A DATE
      `my earnings changed for good` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the earnings change occurred` IS A DATE
      `I took unpaid leave` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of unpaid leave` IS A DATE
      `the day earnings were payable again after leave` IS A DATE
      `COVID-19 changed my arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that change materially reduced my earnings from 23 March to 14 June 2020` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day from 15 June 2020 with earnings payable` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Earning period`
`the adjusted earning period` `the date of my injury` `the day I was first engaged` `my earnings changed for good` `the day the earnings change occurred` `I took unpaid leave` `the first day of unpaid leave` `the day earnings were payable again after leave` `COVID-19 changed my arrangements` `that change materially reduced my earnings from 23 March to 14 June 2020` `the first day from 15 June 2020 with earnings payable` MEANS
    `Earning period` WITH
        `the first day of the period` IS `start after 8C`
        `the last day of the period` IS `period end`
        `days excluded inside it` IS `excluded`
        `days that count` IS ((`the days between` `start after 8C` `and` `period end`) PLUS 1) MINUS `excluded`
    WHERE
        `period end` MEANS `the day` (0 MINUS 1) `days after` `the date of my injury`
        `unadjusted start` MEANS `the day` (0 MINUS 364) `days after` `the date of my injury`
        `start after 8B` MEANS `the later day of` `unadjusted start` `and` `the day I was first engaged`
        `start after 8C` MEANS
            IF     `my earnings changed for good`
               AND `start after 8B` `falls on or before` `the day the earnings change occurred`
               AND `the day the earnings change occurred` `falls on or before` `period end`
            THEN `the day the earnings change occurred`
            ELSE `start after 8B`
        `leave last day` MEANS `the day` (0 MINUS 1) `days after` `the day earnings were payable again after leave`
        `leave days in the period` MEANS `the days shared by` `the first day of unpaid leave` `to` `leave last day` `with` `start after 8C` `to` `period end`
        `cl 8E applies` MEANS
                `I took unpaid leave`
            AND `start after 8C` `falls on or before` `the first day of unpaid leave`
            AND `leave days in the period` AT LEAST 7
        `days A` MEANS IF `cl 8E applies` THEN `leave days in the period` ELSE 0
        `cl 8EA(2) applies` MEANS `COVID-19 changed my arrangements` AND `that change materially reduced my earnings from 23 March to 14 June 2020`
        `days B` MEANS
            IF `cl 8EA(2) applies`
            THEN `the days shared by` `the first prescribed period starts` `to` `the first prescribed period ends` `with` `start after 8C` `to` `period end`
            ELSE 0
        `cl 8EA(3) applies` MEANS
                `cl 8EA(2) applies`
            AND `the days between` `the second prescribed period starts` `and` `the first day from 15 June 2020 with earnings payable` AT LEAST 2
        `second run ends` MEANS `the earlier day of` (`the day` (0 MINUS 1) `days after` `the first day from 15 June 2020 with earnings payable`) `and` `the second prescribed period ends`
        `days C` MEANS
            IF `cl 8EA(3) applies`
            THEN `the days shared by` `the second prescribed period starts` `to` `second run ends` `with` `start after 8C` `to` `period end`
            ELSE 0
        `days A and B` MEANS
            IF `cl 8E applies` AND `cl 8EA(2) applies`
            THEN `the days shared by three runs` `the first day of unpaid leave` `leave last day` `the first prescribed period starts` `the first prescribed period ends` `start after 8C` `period end`
            ELSE 0
        `days A and C` MEANS
            IF `cl 8E applies` AND `cl 8EA(3) applies`
            THEN `the days shared by three runs` `the first day of unpaid leave` `leave last day` `the second prescribed period starts` `second run ends` `start after 8C` `period end`
            ELSE 0
        `excluded` MEANS ((`days A` PLUS `days B`) PLUS `days C`) MINUS (`days A and B` PLUS `days A and C`)

@export What is my relevant earning period for working out my pre-injury average weekly earnings, after the Regulation's adjustments (Regulation cll 8A-8C, 8E, 8EA; 1987 Act Sch 3 cl 2(2))? Gives its first and last day, the days excluded inside it, and the days that count.
GIVEN `the date of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The date you received the injury
      `the day I was first engaged` IS A DATE @desc The day you first started in this employment
      `my earnings changed for good` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the 52 weeks before the injury, your employment arrangement changed in an ongoing way that made a financially material change to your earnings (for example, full-time to part-time)
      `the day the earnings change occurred` IS A DATE @desc The day that change to your earnings occurred (any date if none)
      `I took unpaid leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in that period, you took unpaid leave during which no earnings in this employment were paid or payable to you for at least 7 calendar days in a row from its first day
      `the first day of unpaid leave` IS A DATE @desc The first day of that unpaid leave (any date if none)
      `the day earnings were payable again after leave` IS A DATE @desc The day earnings in this employment once again became payable to you after the leave (any date if none)
      `COVID-19 changed my arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in that period, your employment arrangements changed as a direct result of the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic on your employer's operations or finances
      `that change materially reduced my earnings from 23 March to 14 June 2020` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that change made a financially material reduction to your total earnings between 23 March and 14 June 2020
      `the first day from 15 June 2020 with earnings payable` IS A DATE @desc The first day on or after 15 June 2020 on which earnings in any employment were payable to you (15 June 2020 if you had earnings that day)
GIVETH A MAYBE `Earning period`
`What is my relevant earning period` MEANS
    IF `Part 4 applies to my injury` `the date of my injury`
    THEN JUST (`the adjusted earning period` `the date of my injury` `the day I was first engaged` `my earnings changed for good` `the day the earnings change occurred` `I took unpaid leave` `the first day of unpaid leave` `the day earnings were payable again after leave` `COVID-19 changed my arrangements` `that change materially reduced my earnings from 23 March to 14 June 2020` `the first day from 15 June 2020 with earnings payable`)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (scope limit with "only": cl 8(2) applies Part 4 only to injuries on or after 21 October 2019; earlier injuries fall under Part 3 and the old s 44C kept by the 1987 Act's transitional provisions, not encoded)

-- Sch 3 cl 2(1): "the weekly average of the gross pre-injury earnings received by the worker" in the relevant earning
-- period; with cl 2(4) and cl 8AB, never less than $155. The weekly average is the gross earnings for the days that count
-- times 7, divided by those days (fork F7).
@export What are my pre-injury average weekly earnings in this employment (1987 Act Sch 3 cl 2(1), (2), (4); Regulation cll 8A-8C, 8E, 8EA, 8AB)?
GIVEN `the date of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The date you received the injury
      `the day I was first engaged` IS A DATE @desc The day you first started in this employment
      `my earnings changed for good` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the 52 weeks before the injury, your employment arrangement changed in an ongoing way that made a financially material change to your earnings
      `the day the earnings change occurred` IS A DATE @desc The day that change to your earnings occurred (any date if none)
      `I took unpaid leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in that period, you took unpaid leave with no earnings paid or payable for at least 7 calendar days in a row from its first day
      `the first day of unpaid leave` IS A DATE @desc The first day of that unpaid leave (any date if none)
      `the day earnings were payable again after leave` IS A DATE @desc The day earnings once again became payable to you after the leave (any date if none)
      `COVID-19 changed my arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in that period, your arrangements changed as a direct result of the impact of COVID-19 on your employer
      `that change materially reduced my earnings from 23 March to 14 June 2020` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that change materially reduced your total earnings between 23 March and 14 June 2020
      `the first day from 15 June 2020 with earnings payable` IS A DATE @desc The first day on or after 15 June 2020 on which earnings in any employment were payable to you
      `my gross earnings in the days that count` IS A NUMBER @desc Your gross earnings in this employment for work done on the days of the adjusted relevant earning period that count, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What are my pre-injury average weekly earnings` MEANS
    IF `Part 4 applies to my injury` `the date of my injury`
    THEN IF `the counted days` GREATER THAN 0
         THEN JUST (max `the prescribed minimum PIAWE` ((`my gross earnings in the days that count` TIMES 7) DIVIDED BY `the counted days`))
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: no day of the period counts, e.g. a worker engaged on the day of the injury; Sch 3 cl 4 (short-term workers) and cl 8F then apply)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (scope limit with "only": cl 8(2))
    WHERE
        `the counted days` MEANS (`the adjusted earning period` `the date of my injury` `the day I was first engaged` `my earnings changed for good` `the day the earnings change occurred` `I took unpaid leave` `the first day of unpaid leave` `the day earnings were payable again after leave` `COVID-19 changed my arrangements` `that change materially reduced my earnings from 23 March to 14 June 2020` `the first day from 15 June 2020 with earnings payable`)'s `days that count`

-- cl 8D(1) the period "may be adjusted to align [it] with any regular interval at which the worker is entitled to receive
-- payment"; (2) "is not to be adjusted as provided by this clause unless the insurer is reasonably satisfied that the
-- amount of pre-injury average weekly earnings calculated by reference to the period as so adjusted is not less than the
-- amount that it would have been but for the adjustment."
@export May my relevant earning period be lined up with my pay periods (Regulation cl 8D)?
GIVEN `the date of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The date you received the injury
      `I am paid at regular intervals` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to be paid at a regular interval (for example weekly or fortnightly) in this employment
      `the insurer is reasonably satisfied it would not lower my PIAWE` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer is reasonably satisfied that lining the period up with your pay periods would not give a lower figure than without it
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May my earning period be aligned with my pay` MEANS
    IF `Part 4 applies to my injury` `the date of my injury`
    THEN IF `I am paid at regular intervals` AND `the insurer is reasonably satisfied it would not lower my PIAWE`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- cl 8(2) "This Part applies only to injuries received on or after 21 October 2019": the text's own no

§§ `Part 4 Division 3 -- apprentices, trainees and young people (cl 8G)`

-- cl 8G(1) for Sch 3 cl 5(3)(c): PIAWE are determined "by having regard to the average weekly amount earned during the
-- latest earning stage -- (a) by other persons who have attained the age of 21 years, and (b) for the performance by those
-- persons of similar work as the worker"; (2) "If there are no persons who have attained that age and who are so
-- employed and performing similar work ..., the worker's pre-injury average weekly earnings is the maximum weekly
-- compensation amount." (3) latest earning stage: "the period of 52 weeks before the worker attained the age of 21
-- years". The maximum weekly compensation amount is the 1987 Act s 34 amount, indexed by orders that are not deposited;
-- empty means the deposited figure of $1,838.70.
`the deposited maximum weekly compensation amount` MEANS 1838.70

@export What are my pre-injury average weekly earnings under clause 8G, as an apprentice, trainee or worker under 21 to whom 1987 Act Sch 3 clause 5(3)(c) applies?
GIVEN `Schedule 3 clause 5(3)(c) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your PIAWE fall to be worked out under Sch 3 clause 5(3)(c) of the 1987 Act (you are under 21, an apprentice or a trainee entitled to increments, in the stage that clause covers)
      `people aged 21 or over do similar work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there are people aged 21 or over, employed doing work similar to yours (with your employer or anyone else)
      `their average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The average weekly amount those people earned in the 52 weeks before you turned 21, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the maximum weekly compensation amount` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc The current maximum weekly compensation amount under s 34 of the 1987 Act, if you know it; leave empty to use the figure in the deposited text, $1,838.70
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`My PIAWE as an apprentice, trainee or young worker` MEANS
    IF `Schedule 3 clause 5(3)(c) applies to me`
    THEN IF `people aged 21 or over do similar work`
         THEN JUST `their average weekly earnings`
         ELSE CONSIDER `the maximum weekly compensation amount`
              WHEN JUST `the declared amount` THEN JUST `the declared amount`
              WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST `the deposited maximum weekly compensation amount`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (scope limit with no "only": cl 8G is made "for the purposes of clause 5(3)(c)")

§§ `Part 4 Division 4 -- pre-injury average weekly earnings agreements (cll 8H-8M)`

@export By what date must the application to the insurer to approve our PIAWE agreement be made (Regulation cl 8J(2))?
GIVEN `the day the insurer was first notified of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day of the initial notification of the injury to the insurer
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must our PIAWE agreement application be made` MEANS `the day` 5 `days after` `the day the insurer was first notified of my injury`

@export Was the application to approve our PIAWE agreement made in time, within 5 days of the first notification of my injury (Regulation cl 8J(2))?
GIVEN `the day the insurer was first notified of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day of the initial notification of the injury to the insurer
      `the application has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or your employer have applied in writing to the insurer to approve the agreement
      `the day of the application` IS A DATE @desc The day the application was made (any date if not yet)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`Was our PIAWE agreement application made in time` MEANS
    `the outcome of` `cl 8J(2) -- the application for approval of a PIAWE agreement is to be made within 5 days` `for` `the worker or the employer` `doing` `apply for approval of the agreement` `done` `the application has been made` `on day` (`the day number of` `the day of the application` `from` `the day the insurer was first notified of my injury`) `today being day` (`the day number of` `today` `from` `the day the insurer was first notified of my injury`)

-- cl 8K(11) "person under legal incapacity includes" (a) a child under 18, (b) an involuntary or forensic patient,
-- (c) a person under guardianship, (d) a protected person, (e) an incommunicate person. An open list ("includes"): any
-- other legal incapacity is asked as a fact.
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER
      `I am an involuntary or forensic patient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am under guardianship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a protected person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am an incommunicate person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am otherwise under a legal incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am a person under legal incapacity` `my age` `I am an involuntary or forensic patient` `I am under guardianship` `I am a protected person` `I am an incommunicate person` `I am otherwise under a legal incapacity` IF
       `my age` LESS THAN 18
    OR `I am an involuntary or forensic patient`
    OR `I am under guardianship`
    OR `I am a protected person`
    OR `I am an incommunicate person`
    OR `I am otherwise under a legal incapacity`

-- cl 8K(4) "The insurer is to approve ... if satisfied that the agreed amount reasonably reflects the worker's pre-injury
-- earnings (excluding any earnings before or after the period of 52 weeks ending immediately before the date of the
-- injury) and that the agreement is otherwise fair and reasonable." (5) "must not approve ... a worker who is a person
-- under legal incapacity." (8) "is not to approve ... if, before the application ... was made, the insurer made a work
-- capacity decision about the amount of the worker's pre-injury average weekly earnings." 8H(2) the obligation to
-- determine "ceases if the insurer disputes liability for the weekly payments". 8L(1) "Only one ... agreement may be
-- approved ... in respect of the worker's claim". A late application (not "in accordance with clause 8J", 8K(1)) answers
-- NOTHING (fork F8).
@export Must the insurer approve our PIAWE agreement (Regulation cl 8K(4), (5), (8); cl 8H(2); cl 8L(1))?
GIVEN `the application was made within the 5 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application for approval was made in writing within 5 days after the initial notification of your injury to the insurer
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years
      `I am an involuntary or forensic patient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an involuntary or forensic patient under the Mental Health Act 2007
      `I am under guardianship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are under guardianship under the Guardianship Act 1987
      `I am a protected person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a protected person under the NSW Trustee and Guardian Act 2009
      `I am an incommunicate person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a physical or mental disability prevents you from receiving communications or expressing your will about your property or affairs
      `I am otherwise under a legal incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are under any other legal incapacity
      `the insurer already made a work capacity decision about my PIAWE` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before the application was made, the insurer made a work capacity decision about the amount of your pre-injury average weekly earnings
      `the insurer disputes liability for my weekly payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer disputes liability for your weekly payments of compensation
      `an agreement has already been approved on this claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has already approved a PIAWE agreement on this claim for weekly payments
      `the insurer is satisfied the amount is fair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer is satisfied that the agreed amount reasonably reflects your earnings in the 52 weeks before the injury and that the agreement is otherwise fair and reasonable
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must the insurer approve our PIAWE agreement` MEANS
    IF `I am a person under legal incapacity` `my age` `I am an involuntary or forensic patient` `I am under guardianship` `I am a protected person` `I am an incommunicate person` `I am otherwise under a legal incapacity`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the insurer already made a work capacity decision about my PIAWE`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `the insurer disputes liability for my weekly payments`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE IF `an agreement has already been approved on this claim`
                   THEN JUST FALSE
                   ELSE IF `the application was made within the 5 days`
                        THEN IF `the insurer is satisfied the amount is fair`
                             THEN JUST TRUE
                             ELSE JUST FALSE
                        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: cl 8K(1) ties the duty to an application in accordance with cl 8J; the text does not say a late one may not be approved) (fork F8)

-- cl 8I(1) the PIAWE that apply "is the amount specified in a pre-injury average weekly earnings agreement (if any)
-- approved by the insurer"; (2) subject to the $155 minimum; 8H(3) an approved agreement "ceases to have effect ... if
-- the insurer disputes liability for the weekly payments"; 8M(1) a party may withdraw at any time, and the insurer then
-- determines the amount (8M(2)).
@export What pre-injury average weekly earnings apply to me under our approved PIAWE agreement (Regulation cll 8I, 8H(3), 8M)?
GIVEN `the insurer approved our agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer approved the PIAWE agreement between you and your employer
      `the agreed amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly amount in the agreement, in dollars
      `the insurer disputes liability for my weekly payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer disputes liability for your weekly payments of compensation
      `a party has withdrawn from the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or your employer have withdrawn from the agreement by written notice
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What PIAWE apply under our agreement` MEANS
    IF     `the insurer approved our agreement`
       AND (NOT `the insurer disputes liability for my weekly payments`)
       AND (NOT `a party has withdrawn from the agreement`)
    THEN JUST (max `the prescribed minimum PIAWE` `the agreed amount`)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: without an agreement in effect the PIAWE are worked out under Sch 3 or determined by the insurer under cl 8M(2))

-- cl 8L(2) "However, the insurer may approve a variation of the pre-injury average weekly earnings agreement on the
-- application of the worker or the employer if the worker's entitlement to the use of a non-monetary benefit has been
-- withdrawn on or after the date of the injury concerned."
@export May the insurer approve a variation of our approved PIAWE agreement (Regulation cl 8L)?
GIVEN `the date of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The date you received the injury
      `a non-monetary benefit of mine was withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your entitlement to use a non-monetary benefit (for example a car, housing or a phone) has been withdrawn
      `the day it was withdrawn` IS A DATE @desc The day that entitlement was withdrawn (any date if not)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May the insurer approve a variation of our agreement` MEANS
    IF `a non-monetary benefit of mine was withdrawn` AND `the date of my injury` `falls on or before` `the day it was withdrawn`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- cl 8K(2) 7 days after receiving the application; (3) "If the insurer has a reasonable excuse for not commencing
-- provisional weekly payments ..., the insurer is to determine the application within 7 days after the earlier of ...
-- (a) the insurer ceases to have a reasonable excuse ..., (b) the insurer accepts liability for weekly payments". Day 0
-- is the day of receipt, or under (3) the earlier of those two days (fork F9: even if it is before receipt).
GIVEN `the day the insurer received the application` IS A DATE
      `the insurer has a reasonable excuse for not starting provisional payments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the excuse has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the excuse ended` IS A DATE
      `the insurer has accepted liability for weekly payments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it accepted liability` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day the 7 days to determine run from` `the day the insurer received the application` `the insurer has a reasonable excuse for not starting provisional payments` `the excuse has ended` `the day the excuse ended` `the insurer has accepted liability for weekly payments` `the day it accepted liability` MEANS
    IF `the insurer has a reasonable excuse for not starting provisional payments`
    THEN IF `the excuse has ended` AND `the insurer has accepted liability for weekly payments`
         THEN JUST (`the earlier day of` `the day the excuse ended` `and` `the day it accepted liability`)
         ELSE IF `the excuse has ended`
              THEN JUST `the day the excuse ended`
              ELSE IF `the insurer has accepted liability for weekly payments`
                   THEN JUST `the day it accepted liability`
                   ELSE NOTHING
    ELSE JUST `the day the insurer received the application`

@export By what date must the insurer decide whether to approve our PIAWE agreement (Regulation cl 8K(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the day the insurer received the application` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer received the application for approval
      `the insurer has a reasonable excuse for not starting provisional payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has a reasonable excuse for not starting provisional weekly payments
      `the excuse has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has stopped having that reasonable excuse
      `the day the excuse ended` IS A DATE @desc The day it stopped having the excuse (any date if not)
      `the insurer has accepted liability for weekly payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has accepted liability for weekly payments for the injury
      `the day it accepted liability` IS A DATE @desc The day it accepted liability (any date if not)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By when must the insurer decide our PIAWE agreement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the 7 days to determine run from` `the day the insurer received the application` `the insurer has a reasonable excuse for not starting provisional payments` `the excuse has ended` `the day the excuse ended` `the insurer has accepted liability for weekly payments` `the day it accepted liability`
    WHEN JUST `the start day` THEN JUST (`the day` 7 `days after` `the start day`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: under cl 8K(3) the 7 days have not started while the excuse lasts and liability is not accepted)

@export Has the insurer decided our PIAWE agreement application in time (Regulation cl 8K(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the day the insurer received the application` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer received the application for approval
      `the insurer has a reasonable excuse for not starting provisional payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has a reasonable excuse for not starting provisional weekly payments
      `the excuse has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has stopped having that reasonable excuse
      `the day the excuse ended` IS A DATE @desc The day it stopped having the excuse (any date if not)
      `the insurer has accepted liability for weekly payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has accepted liability for weekly payments for the injury
      `the day it accepted liability` IS A DATE @desc The day it accepted liability (any date if not)
      `the insurer has decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has decided to approve or refuse the agreement
      `the day it decided` IS A DATE @desc The day it decided (any date if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A MAYBE `What became of the duty`
`Has the insurer decided our PIAWE agreement in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the 7 days to determine run from` `the day the insurer received the application` `the insurer has a reasonable excuse for not starting provisional payments` `the excuse has ended` `the day the excuse ended` `the insurer has accepted liability for weekly payments` `the day it accepted liability`
    WHEN JUST `the start day` THEN JUST (`the outcome of` `cl 8K(2), (3) -- the insurer is to determine the application within 7 days` `for` `the insurer` `doing` `determine the application` `done` `the insurer has decided` `on day` (`the day number of` `the day it decided` `from` `the start day`) `today being day` (`the day number of` `today` `from` `the start day`))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: cl 8K(3), the 7 days have not started)

@export By what date must the insurer work out my PIAWE and tell me, after a withdrawal from our PIAWE agreement (Regulation cl 8M(2))?
GIVEN `the day the insurer received the notice of withdrawal` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer received written notice that you or your employer withdrew from the approved agreement
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the insurer act on the withdrawal` MEANS `the day` 7 `days after` `the day the insurer received the notice of withdrawal`

@export Has the insurer worked out my PIAWE and given notice in time after the withdrawal from our PIAWE agreement (Regulation cl 8M(2))?
GIVEN `the day the insurer received the notice of withdrawal` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer received written notice of the withdrawal
      `the insurer has given notice of the amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has given you and your employer written notice of the withdrawal and of the PIAWE amount it determined
      `the day of that notice` IS A DATE @desc The day of that notice (any date if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`Has the insurer acted on the withdrawal in time` MEANS
    `the outcome of` `cl 8M(2) -- the insurer is to determine the earnings and give notice within 7 days of a withdrawal` `for` `the insurer` `doing` `determine the earnings and give notice of the withdrawal` `done` `the insurer has given notice of the amount` `on day` (`the day number of` `the day of that notice` `from` `the day the insurer received the notice of withdrawal`) `today being day` (`the day number of` `today` `from` `the day the insurer received the notice of withdrawal`)

§§ `Part 4 Division 5 -- paying an increase (cl 8N)`

-- cl 8N(2) "A payment increase decision is a work capacity decision about the amount of a worker's pre-injury average
-- weekly earnings or current weekly earnings that results in an increase in the amount of weekly payments of
-- compensation becoming payable to the worker in respect of any period before the decision is made."
@export Is the insurer's decision a "payment increase decision" that it must pay within 14 days (Regulation cl 8N(2))?
GIVEN `it is a work capacity decision about my PIAWE or current weekly earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision is a work capacity decision about the amount of your pre-injury average weekly earnings or your current weekly earnings
      `it increases what I am owed for a period before the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision makes a higher weekly payment payable to you for some period before the decision was made
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is it a payment increase decision` MEANS
    IF `it is a work capacity decision about my PIAWE or current weekly earnings` AND `it increases what I am owed for a period before the decision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@export By what date must the insurer pay me the increase after a payment increase decision (Regulation cl 8N(1))?
GIVEN `the day of the payment increase decision` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer made the payment increase decision
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the insurer pay the increase` MEANS `the day` 14 `days after` `the day of the payment increase decision`

@export Has the insurer paid me the increase in time, within 14 days of its payment increase decision (Regulation cl 8N(1))? Late payment is an offence (maximum 20 penalty units).
GIVEN `the day of the payment increase decision` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer made the payment increase decision
      `the increase has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has paid you the amount of the increase for the earlier period
      `the day it was paid` IS A DATE @desc The day it was paid (any date if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`Has the insurer paid the increase in time` MEANS
    `the outcome of` `cl 8N(1) -- the insurer must pay the increase within 14 days of a payment increase decision` `for` `the insurer` `doing` `pay the increase` `done` `the increase has been paid` `on day` (`the day number of` `the day it was paid` `from` `the day of the payment increase decision`) `today being day` (`the day number of` `today` `from` `the day of the payment increase decision`)

§§ `Part 5 -- return to work assistance (cll 9, 10)`

-- cl 9(1) "a pre-injury employer is not liable to pay compensation for the cost of work assistance provided to assist a
-- worker to return to work with a new employer if -- (a) the offer of employment with the new employer is an offer of
-- employment for a period of less than 3 months, or (b) the offer of employment has not been made in writing."
-- "Less than 3 months": the offered period ends before the day before the same date three months on (fork F10).
@export Does clause 9 rule out compensation for work assistance to help me start with a new employer (Regulation cl 9(1); 1987 Act s 64B)? A no means clause 9 does not stop it; s 64B decides the rest.
GIVEN `the offer was made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the new employer's offer of employment was made in writing
      `the offer has an end date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offered employment is for a fixed period (no if it is ongoing)
      `the first day of the offered employment` IS A DATE @desc The first day of the offered employment
      `the last day of the offered employment` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the offered employment (any date if ongoing)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does clause 9 rule out work assistance` MEANS
    IF `the offer was made in writing`
    THEN     `the offer has an end date`
         AND ((`the day` 1 `days after` `the last day of the offered employment`) `falls before` (`the day` 3 `months after` `the first day of the offered employment`))
    ELSE TRUE

DECLARE `Training provider` IS ONE OF
    `an NVR registered training organisation`
    `a registered higher education provider`
    `another person or body`

-- cl 10(1) "an employer is not liable to pay compensation for the cost of education or training provided to assist a
-- worker to return to work if -- (a) the provision of the education or training is inconsistent with the retraining or
-- employment objectives of the injury management plan established for the worker, or (b) the education or training is
-- provided by any person or body other than -- (i) an NVR registered training organisation ..., or (ii) a registered
-- higher education provider ...".
@export Does clause 10 rule out compensation for education or training to help me return to work (Regulation cl 10(1); 1987 Act s 64C)? A no means clause 10 does not stop it; s 64C decides the rest.
GIVEN `it is inconsistent with my injury management plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the education or training is inconsistent with the retraining or employment objectives of your injury management plan
      `the provider` IS A `Training provider` @desc Who provides it: an NVR registered training organisation, a registered higher education provider (TEQSA), or another person or body
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does clause 10 rule out education or training` MEANS
    IF `it is inconsistent with my injury management plan`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the provider`
         WHEN `another person or body` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE

@export By what date must my claim for return to work assistance be accepted or disputed (Regulation cl 9(2): work assistance, 14 days; cl 10(2): education or training, 21 days)?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Return to work claim` @desc Which claim: work assistance with a new employer (s 64B), or education or training (s 64C)
      `the day I made the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you made the claim
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must my return to work claim be decided` MEANS `the day` (`the days to determine` `the claim`) `days after` `the day I made the claim`

@export Has my claim for return to work assistance been accepted or disputed in time (Regulation cl 9(2), cl 10(2))?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Return to work claim` @desc Which claim: work assistance with a new employer (s 64B), or education or training (s 64C)
      `the day I made the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you made the claim
      `it has been determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person you claimed from has accepted or disputed liability
      `the day it was determined` IS A DATE @desc The day it accepted or disputed liability (any date if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`Has my return to work claim been decided in time` MEANS
    `the outcome of` (`cl 9(2), 10(2) -- the claim must be determined within 14 or 21 days` `the claim`) `for` `the person the claim is made on` `doing` `determine the claim by accepting or disputing liability` `done` `it has been determined` `on day` (`the day number of` `the day it was determined` `from` `the day I made the claim`) `today being day` (`the day number of` `today` `from` `the day I made the claim`)
